/Title (Who we served Our 396 clients reflected the rich diversity of our communities. 60% identified as female and 40% as male. By ethnicity, 43% identified as White, 12% as Asian/Asian British, 11% as Black/African/Caribbean, and 9% as Mixed heritage. The most common concerns bringing clients to us were anxiety \(28%\), emotional and behavioural difficulties \(21%\), and low mood \(13%\), alongside family changes, bereavement and trauma.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2361 0 R
/Next 2562 0 R
>>
endobj
